Tells the core (//browser_core/drm_request.mojom) how a page's request for a protected-media key
system was answered, so the app can say why a site's video won't play, and say nothing once it
plays. requestMediaKeySystemAccess is answered in the renderer, and the browser never hears of it:
its initializer, made on the Blink encrypted media module's initializer base, calls the core's
per-frame interface with the answer, and the core adds its binder to a frame's through
g_browser_core_populate_frame_binders (//browser_core/hooks.h). What an answer means is the core's
to decide; nothing comes back.

